CERTORA VERIFICATION MUNGE — NegRiskModule._storeResult virtual seam
=====================================================================
`NegRiskModuleHarness` overrides `_storeResult` to mirror stored results into
uint256-keyed mappings that CVL hooks can observe (r0Mirror, r1Mirror,
lenMirror, yesSumMirror). The production `NegRiskModule._storeResult` is
declared `internal override` (non-virtual), which seals the inheritance chain
and blocks the harness override from compiling.

This munge adds `virtual` so `NegRiskModuleHarness._storeResult ... override`
compiles. Production behavior is identical: no production contract subclasses
NegRiskModule.

Required by: every NegRisk-* conf and eq/NegRiskMigrationEquivalence (they
compile NegRiskModuleHarness, whose `_storeResult` override needs the base
`virtual`).
Apply:  git apply certora/patches/NegRiskModule_storeResultVirtual.patch
Revert: git apply -R certora/patches/NegRiskModule_storeResultVirtual.patch
Never commit the applied state to src/.

diff --git a/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol b/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
index c3d9e1b..e822eca 100644
--- a/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
+++ b/src/modules/NegRiskModule.sol
@@ -382,7 +382,7 @@ contract NegRiskModule is UUPSUpgradeable, Initializable, BaseModule, NegRiskMig
     }
 
     /// @dev Neg-risk conditions are binary: every condition resolves fully YES or fully NO.
-    function _storeResult(ConditionId _conditionId, uint256[] memory _result) internal override {
+    function _storeResult(ConditionId _conditionId, uint256[] memory _result) internal virtual override {
         super._storeResult(_conditionId, _result);
 
         uint256 result0 = _result[0];
